<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 8.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 8.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Tuesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    357.14  2.25</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	    217.27  3.02</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	 183.66  8.32</p>
<p> 4   Colonial Coml	  122.95  2.25</p>
<p> 5   Adel Bton Cement     118.84  1.64</p>
<p> 6   Herald Rsc		92.04  1.04</p>
<p> 7   Westral Forest	  85.14  2.35</p>
<p> 8   Forrestania Gold	83.87  2.34</p>
<p> 9   Countrywide-PP	  83.21  1.14</p>
<p>10   Energy Equity	   71.94  1.00</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		 1.98  0.86</p>
<p> 2 Consol Rutile		2.97  0.84</p>
<p> 3 Computer Power	     3.76  3.85</p>
<p> 4 Premier Inv		  4.23  0.75</p>
<p> 5 Queensland Cotton	  5.85  4.44</p>
<p> 6 Parbury Ltd		  6.25  0.74</p>
<p> 7 BTR Plc			6.56  6.10</p>
<p> 8 OLS Asia Hldgs	     7.06  0.84</p>
<p> 9 Aust Gold Rsc		7.40  1.35</p>
<p>10 FAI Life ltd		 7.67  0.79</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
